# act — https://github.com/nektos/act. Ported from resume-2026 (M0.23).
#
# catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest is the closest public match to GitHub's
# hosted Ubuntu runner and ships multi-arch (amd64 + arm64), so it also runs
# unmodified on Apple Silicon. The labels on the left are the ones the
# workflows pin in `runs-on:` — ubuntu-26.04 everywhere since MB.37, not the
# floating ubuntu-latest, and Blacksmith's for vitest.yml since MB.96. A label
# with no line here leaves act no platform for its job, so bump them together.
# --pull=false leaves the first-use pull to docker and skips a redundant
# registry round-trip on every later run.
-P ubuntu-26.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P blacksmith-8vcpu-ubuntu-2404=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
--pull=false
